00:15.204   Allocation    GlyphAtlas texture   66.00 MiB
00:15.212   Allocation    buffer               64.00 MiB
00:15.268   Deallocation  buffer               64.00 MiB  56 ms
00:15.268   Deallocation  GlyphAtlas texture   33.00 MiB  5.29 s
00:26.973   Allocation    GlyphAtlas texture    4.12 MiB          <- reset at max size
00:26.980   Deallocation  GlyphAtlas texture   66.00 MiB  11.78 s
...
00:35.333   Allocation    GlyphAtlas texture   66.00 MiB          <- second cycle
00:35.335   Allocation    buffer               64.00 MiB
```

So at the 33 → 66 MiB step, the old atlas (33), the new atlas (66) and the 64 MiB buffer are live at the same time: ~163 MiB just for glyph caching.

Behaviour observed with the size sequence:
- Revisiting a size (back to 18, then 22) does not grow memory further.
- Moving to 26 lowers the footprint, which matches the atlas being reset once it hits the max size.

I see the same pattern in a real reading UI (paged text, CJK book). A footprint peak of ~396 MB on this device is about 12% of its measured jetsam limit, so it is fine there. The concern is devices with less RAM: the atlas cap is the same 16384 px on every Apple3+ GPU (A9 and later), including 2 GB devices.

