### Expected results

The semantics label is `second`, so a screen reader announces the new label.

### Actual results

The label stays `first`. The same happens when only `locale` changes (the `LocaleStringAttribute` keeps the old locale), and for `semanticsIdentifier` and `spellOut`.

`TextSpan.compareTo` only looks at `recognizer` for metadata changes, so it returns `RenderComparison.identical` and `RenderParagraph.text` returns early. `TextSpan.==` and `hashCode` also ignore `locale` and `spellOut`. Separately, the `metadata` branch of `RenderParagraph.text` doesn't clear `_cachedAttributedLabels`, so even a `metadata` result would keep the old label.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Create a new app with `flutter create` and replace `lib/main.dart` with the code sample below (no packages, no images, no assets).
2. Build in profile mode for 32-bit ARM: `flutter build apk --profile --target-platform android-arm`, then install it on a device without Vulkan. The device below is an Android 11 tablet with a Rockchip RK3326 and a Mali-G31 GPU. `pm list features` reports no `vulkan` entry, so Impeller falls back to OpenGLES.
3. Set all three Android animation scales to 1. Launch the app normally (Impeller OpenGLES), then again with Impeller disabled: `adb shell am start -S -n <package>/.MainActivity --ez enable-impeller false`.
4. On each tab ("Cards", "Text"), scroll with identical adb swipes (`adb shell input swipe 300 820 300 300 180`, 4 down then 4 up, 1.1 s apart). Do 3 passes per tab, each starting from a fresh mount of the tab. Collect `FrameTiming` from the VM service (`Flutter.Frame` events on the `Extension` stream) during each pass.

### Expected results

On a device where OpenGLES is the only Impeller backend, raster time should be in the same range as Skia. Skia is the engine Impeller replaces, and the opt-out is deprecated (the engine logs `Impeller opt-out deprecated ... please report a bug`).

### Actual results

Impeller OpenGLES has about **1.9x the median raster time** of Skia on the same APK, for both a simple card list and a plain text page. The gap is the same on 3.44.3 stable, 3.50.0-0.3.pre beta and current master. Both build times stay under 2 ms, so the difference is on the raster thread.

About 1,100 frames per row (3 passes × 8 swipes). "Frames > 16.7 ms" counts frames where build or raster exceeds the 60 Hz budget.

