The gap is not caused by any single widget. A page containing nothing but text costs as much raster time under Impeller as the card list. This repro stays mostly within budget because it is deliberately minimal. In a production app on the same device, card lists with a few more draw calls take 21-24 ms of raster per frame under Impeller OpenGLES, so 100 % of frames are janky. The same APK under Skia takes 6-7 ms, with 1-6 % janky frames. A timeline of that app is dominated by `ReactorGLES::React`, at about 15 ms per frame.

The fix for #192147 (GL state re-emitted on every draw, fixed by #193427, already in 3.50 beta) does not change these numbers on this GPU.

Related: #192364 (Adreno 702, open) · #193009 (PowerVR GE8320, closed for lack of a minimal repro; this issue provides one) · #192147 / #193427 · #187009 (Adreno 506) · #190195.

