### Steps to reproduce

1. Use a device where Impeller selects OpenGL ES. Ours is a Samsung Galaxy A22 (SM-A225F, MediaTek MT6768 / Mali-G52, Android 13, vendor API 31): `android_context_dynamic_impeller.cc` avoids Vulkan on MediaTek below vendor API 32, and logcat shows `Using the Impeller rendering backend (OpenGLES).`
2. Enable Flutter GPU (`io.flutter.embedding.android.EnableFlutterGPU` = true in AndroidManifest.xml, and `--enable-flutter-gpu`).
3. Run the integration test below on the device: `flutter test integration_test/probe_test.dart -d <device> --enable-flutter-gpu`.

### Expected results

The texture cleared by the render pass reads back its clear color (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1). The same kind of clear pass, in our renderer, reads back correctly on Metal (macOS desktop, iOS simulator).

### Actual results

```
formats: color PixelFormat.r8g8b8a8UNormInt, depth PixelFormat.d24UnormS8Uint
upload then readback: [10, 20, 30, 255]
clear pass then readback: [0, 0, 0, 0]
```

Uploading with `Texture.overwrite` and reading back through `asImage()` works, so readback itself works. A render pass leaves its color attachment untouched, though: not even the clear is applied. The result is the same with `StorageMode.devicePrivate` and `StorageMode.hostVisible`, and also after waiting for `submit(completionCallback:)` to complete. Render passes with draw calls also produce all-zero attachments.

